{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Let them bring.</b> The attendants." "<b>and who has set the royal crown on its head.</b> Some say he sensed that the king was displeased concerning the royal crown on account of the honor of the kingship; therefore he said, \"and let the garment and the horse be given,\" and did not mention the crown. But the correct view in my eyes is that the vav in <b>בראשו</b> (on its head) refers back to the horse, for there is a horse of the king upon which they place a royal crown on its head when the king rides upon it, and none of the king's servants is permitted to ride upon it, and this is a well-known matter."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:09.558990661Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}